  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250. The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l as the best image encoder, multiprofile over single, transformer aggregation over avgpool, and weighted over concat fusion. Config_036 (same backbone but avgpool + concat) is the only remaining untested cell in the 2×2 aggregation×fusion grid for this best architecture. While it is unlikely to surpass 0.7250, it completes the design-space comparison, confirming that both transformer aggregation and weighted fusion contribute to the peak performance. As the final experiment with no budget remaining, this is the most informative exploitation choice: it validates the ranking of aggregation and fusion effects within the best model family rather than chasing a low-probability alternative encoder that the RNA-only and image-only evidence already disfavors."
}

